WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.403
-As President Biden was abroad

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.572
trying to restore America's
relationship with key allies,

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:08.341
we found out about
yet another bombshell scandal

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.010
from the Trump era in which
Trump's Justice Department

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.045
spied on Democratic lawmakers

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:15.047
who were investigating him
during the Russia probe.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:18.118
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.389
President Biden
is currently abroad

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.358
for his first major
international trip,

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.660
meeting with leaders
of the G7 and NATO

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.463
and trying to reassure allies
that America is back

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.431
after four years
of erratic leadership.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:35.235
From a guy who once
literally shoved his way

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.770
past a bunch of world leaders
at a NATO summit

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.673
like a maid of honor trying to
catch the bouquet at a wedding.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.342
"You've already
been married twice, Becky.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.542
I need this.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.378
Because some of us are hard
to love, Becky!"

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:47.680
Compare that to Biden,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.516
who was amicably chatting it up
with world leaders

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.252
and at one case even walked
behind the rest of the group

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.021
like a grandpa at Disney World.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.122
"You guys go ahead.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.857
I'm gonna ride the tram
back and forth

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.492
to the parking lot
until you're done.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.627
I like looking at the cars.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.062
That's my Epcot."

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.531
Biden's message at these
meetings has been simple --

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.901
America is back,
you know, like the McRib.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.636
America's back.
For a limited time only.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.937
Offer not valid in Florida.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.672
Although if were
a foreign leader,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.108
you know, I would take it
with a grain of salt.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.377
I mean, yes,
Biden is president now,

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.579
but America definitely
has a split personality.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.580
And who knows how long
this one's gonna last?

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.117
If Dr. Jekyll said, "I'm back,"
it would be fair to ask

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.753
if he threw away the serum
that turned him into Mr. Hyde.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:30.189
And if he responded, "The
important thing is I'm back,

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.425
relax,"
I'm not sure would you relax.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.394
Still, Biden's message
seems to be working.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.796
French president
Emmanuel Macron, for example,

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.332
seemed very excited to have
an American president

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.735
willing to work with European
allies to solve common problems.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:48.240 line:0%
-We have to deal with this
pandemic and the COVID-19.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.877 line:0%
We have to face a lot
of changes, a lot of crisis,

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.512 line:0%
climate change,

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:57.050 line:0%
and for all these issues,
what we need is cooperation.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.354 line:0%
And I think it's great
to have a U.S. president

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:05.992 line:0%
part of the club
and very willing to cooperate.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:09.295 line:0%
And I think that
what you demonstrate

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.998 line:0%
is that leadership
is partnership.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.077
-It's nice to hear some optimism
for a change.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:27.746
Usually when you hear a French
guy say America is back,

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:29.615
it's because
he's watching someone

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:32.051
take picture of the "Mona Lisa"
with an iPad.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.653
[ French accent ]
Oh, great, America is back

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:37.389
with their Crocs and their
Bart Simpson T-shirts.

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:41.293
It is I that say "ay caramba"
to this.

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:43.562
[ Normal voice ] Also,
watching those two pal around

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.230
must be a real burn for Trump.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.266
He was so desperate
to be friends with Macron,

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.868
he shook his hand like he was
trying to get a candy machine

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.337
to drop his PayDay bar

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.674
and held on longer than someone
falling out of a helicopter.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.175
And then, of course,
there was the time

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:57.943
Trump was so nervous
to be with Macron,

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.179
he brushed dandruff
off his shoulder.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.748
[ As Donald Trump ]
You have a booger in your nose.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.515
Mind if I get that for you?

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:06.986
Garçon, can you bring us
your smallest spoon?

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:10.990
[ French accent ] Ugh.
America is back.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.826
You do the Bartman.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.761
[ Normal voice ]
That said, Biden's trip

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.197
has had its
awkward moments, too.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:21.834
For one, there was that awkward
socially distanced picture

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.003
of the G7 leaders
where they look like

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.038
"Street Fighter" characters
no one wants to pick.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:28.674
They should all be doing
that video game character thing

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:31.710
where they bounced in place
in their signature pose.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.579
Biden just standing there
with his dukes up.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.281
And every time
you hover over him,

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.950
he says his catchphrase --
"Come on, man."

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.586
Then there was an odd moment
where a reporter asked Biden

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.721
about some Trump-era
trade policies

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.056
he hasn't rolled back yet.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.492
And Biden, well,
he seemed a little irked.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.364 line:0%
-Yes.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.532
-At the same time,
you've kept in place

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.468
some Trump-era steel
and aluminum sanctions.

00:03:56.468 --> 00:03:57.937
And I wanted to ask you,

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.705
when you're having
these conversations

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.874
with European allies

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.143
who are very concerned
about these sanctions,

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.945
how do you justify that?

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.079
And what are your plans to --

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:10.382
-120 days.
Give me a break.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:11.850
Need time.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:16.455
-Why does he sound like Superman
holding a rod of Kryptonite?

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:18.691
[ Strained voice ] Need time.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:23.596
Must bring...America back.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.231
[ Normal voice ] The point is,
Biden's trying

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.766
to leave the Trump era behind
on the world stage

00:04:27.766 --> 00:04:30.236
even as the GOP tries
to keep it alive here at home

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.805
either by recommitting
themselves to Trumpism

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.608
or by trying to whitewash the
many lies and abuses of power.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.810 line:0%
Trump's former press secretary
Kayleigh McEnany,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.578 line:0%
for example,
said this on Sunday.

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:40.913 line:0%
-And then there was
the question,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.548 line:0%
"Will you ever lie to us?"

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.450 line:0%
And I said,
without hesitation, no.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.751 line:0%
And I never did.

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:46.952 line:0%
I never lied.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.688 line:0%
I sourced my information,

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.892 line:0%
but that will never stop the
press from calling you a liar.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.728
-Wow, it's impressive
to lie about lying.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:58.698
It's like stabbing a witness
during your murder trial.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.667
We shouldn't care what a proven
liar has to say about anything,

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.602
especially the question
of whether she lied or not.

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.571
I mean, no one asks Vanilla Ice

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.573
to come up with an original beat
anymore.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.742
Listening to McEnany explain
how she didn't lie

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.344
is like listening to Ice explain

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:13.746
how his song was different
from "Under Pressure."

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.415
-Like, it goes, ding-ding-ding
diggy ding ding,

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:18.217
ding-ding-ding diggy ding ding.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.385
That's the way theirs goes.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.554
Ours goes, ding-ding-ding
diggy ding ding tch,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.255
ding-ding-ding-ding
diggy ding ding.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:25.624
That little bitty "ting."
It's not the same.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:26.859
-Yeah.
It's not the same.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.561
That's how I sound
explaining the difference

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:32.130
between my Werner Herzog
and Christoph Waltz impressions.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.934
Except that I'm right.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.768
The difference is subtle,
but it's there.

00:05:36.768 --> 00:05:39.238
Werner's like [As Werner]
"The clock is ticking."

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.839
And Christoph's like
[As Christoph] "Yes!

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:42.641
The clock is ticking!"

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:46.012
[ Normal voice ] Look,
if you can't hear difference

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:49.949
between German and Austrian,
then that's on you.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:52.151
Ding, ding-ding di-di-ding-ding.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.487
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.789
Now, obviously,
we could spend all day

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:59.558
laying out McEnany's
most egregious lies,

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.427
like the time she defended
Trump's claim

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.695
that COVID would disappear

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:05.665 line:0%
and described the resurgence
of cases as "embers"

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:08.534
or the time she went on TV
with binders full of bull[bleep]

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.404
to spread the big lie that there
was fraud in the 2020 election.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.906
If you ask me,
she should be the one

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.908
doing a weekly digital segment
called "Corrections"

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:19.778
where she has to defend herself
from hoards of Internet jackals

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.146
critiquing her every utterance.

00:06:21.146 --> 00:06:23.649 line:0%
Oh, and as a reminder,
don't miss "Corrections,"

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.584 line:0%
available every Friday morning
online.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:29.388 line:0%
"Corrections,"
it's a massive waste of time.

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.190
McEnany and the rest
of the Trump crowd

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.359
are eager to rewrite the history
of the Trump era,

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.461
whether it's COVID
or the 2020 election

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.529
or the January 6th insurrection.

00:06:37.529 --> 00:06:39.665
And that's because it's still
very much Trump's party.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:43.268
In fact, one thing that's become
clear about the post-Trump era

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.338
is that if the GOP
gets their way,

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.072
there won't be a post-Trump era.

00:06:47.072 --> 00:06:48.707
The Republican Party
remains deeply committed

00:06:48.707 --> 00:06:49.876
to both the ideology

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:51.744
and the cult of personality
that is Trumpism.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:54.446
Last week, for example, the
number-three House Republican,

00:06:54.446 --> 00:06:56.916
Elise Stefanik,
who just replaced Liz Cheney

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.518
after Cheney criticized Trump
for inciting an insurrection,

00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:01.187
posted a photo of herself
with Trump

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:03.288
and the caption, "Save America."

00:07:03.288 --> 00:07:06.158
"Save Amer--" I wouldn't count
on Trump to save a drowning man

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:09.228
if he was standing in
a life boat filled with buoys.

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.831
[ As Donald Trump ] They're
100 bucks each or two for $200.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.066
That's a great deal.
What's that?

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.369
I can't hear you with all
that water in your mouth.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:19.071
[ Normal voice ] It's not an
encouraging sign for the health
of our democracy

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.440
that the GOP's biggest names
and rising stars

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.908
are happily posing for photos

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:25.077
with the deeply unpopular
autocrat

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.646
who's still lying
about the election

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:28.680
and sowed a violent insurrection
to stay in power.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.249
It's like the captain
of your cruise shipment

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.217
posing for a pic with an iceberg

00:07:32.217 --> 00:07:34.520 line:0%
and the caption,
"Great running into you."

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.288 line:0%
And it's not like
they're just winking

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:37.656
and trying to be subtle
about it.

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:40.125
The GOP has been explicit
that the twice-impeached Trump,

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:41.793
who never once
won the popular vote

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:43.963
and continues to be
deeply unpopular in polls,

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.331
is the leader of their party.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.333
And they've made it clear
they don't want him to go away.

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.735 line:0%
-We are a pro-America
populist party

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:53.472 line:0%
rooted in conservative principle
with Donald Trump as our leader.

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:55.908 line:0%
-It's impossible for this party
to move forward

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:58.811 line:0%
without President Trump
being its leader.

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:00.646
-They look at Donald J. Trump

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:05.217
and they look at the millions
and millions of people inspired

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:08.386
who went to battle fighting
alongside President Trump,

00:08:08.386 --> 00:08:11.490
and they're terrified.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.525
And they want him to go away.

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:15.060
Let me tell you this right now.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.162
Donald J. Trump
ain't going anywhere.

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:19.665
-Ted Cruz's normal voice
is deeply grating,

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.199
but when he tries
to fire up a crowd,

00:08:21.199 --> 00:08:23.836
it's like watching an accordion
player bust out a kazoo.

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:26.739
If Ted Cruz has given the speech
at the end of "Braveheart,"

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:27.874
the Scottish army would have

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.075
just laid down their arms
and gone home.

00:08:30.075 --> 00:08:33.378
[ Scottish accent ] Oh,
I don't care for him at all.

00:08:33.378 --> 00:08:34.980
[ Normal voice ]
It's like that, Lloyd.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.682
That's how it's
supposed to sound.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:38.684
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.789
The Republican Party
has made clear

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.858
that if it gets back into power
in 2022 or 2024,

00:08:46.858 --> 00:08:49.194
they'll follow in Trump's
footsteps, which is terrifying

00:08:49.194 --> 00:08:50.663
and why it's
all the more important

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:52.565
for us to take
a thorough accounting

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:53.832
of Trump's many abuses of power.

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:54.901
Last week, for example,

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:57.169
we learned of yet another
shocking scandal.

00:08:57.169 --> 00:09:00.439
The Trump DOJ sought the private
communication records

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.941
of Democrats who were
investigating the president.

00:09:02.941 --> 00:09:04.510 line:0%
-This is the headline tonight
in "The New York Times"...

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:13.452
...meaning members of Congress
who are Democrats.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:15.321
"As the Justice Department
investigated

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:17.723
who was behind leaks
of classified information

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:18.958
early in
the Trump administration,

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.926
it took highly unusual step.

00:09:20.926 --> 00:09:24.530
Prosecutors subpoenaed Apple,"
the company Apple,

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.431
"for data from the accounts

00:09:26.431 --> 00:09:29.568
of at least two
Democratic members of Congress

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:31.537
on the House
Intelligence Committee

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:34.606
and staffers and family members.

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:37.576
One of those family members
was a child, a minor."

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:38.811
According to committee officials

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:40.346
and two other people
briefed on the inquiry,

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:43.115
all told, the records
of at least a dozen people

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:46.085
tied to the Intelligence
Committee were seized

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:48.420
in 2017 and early 2018,

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.423
including the records
of Congressman Adam Schiff

00:09:51.423 --> 00:09:53.825
of California,
who was then the top Democrat

00:09:53.825 --> 00:09:55.294
on the House
Intelligence Committee

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:57.763
who is now the chairman
of that committee.

00:09:57.763 --> 00:10:00.166
Prosecutors,
under the beleaguered

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:01.934
Trump attorney general
Jeff Sessions,

00:10:01.934 --> 00:10:05.704
were hunting for the sources
behind news media reports

00:10:05.704 --> 00:10:09.375
about contacts between
Trump associates and Russia.

00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:11.610
-Every time you think we're done
with Trump scandals,

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.944
there's a new bombshell.

00:10:12.944 --> 00:10:14.947
40 years from now, I'm gonna
be sitting at this desk

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.515
with long gray hair tied back

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:18.751
in one of those cool
old-man buns

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:21.420
with cataract glasses
and a doughnut cushion

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.055
talking about
the latest Trump scandal,

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:25.557
like how CNN is reporting
that President Trump

00:10:25.557 --> 00:10:28.027
ordered the space force to nuke
every dog in the country.

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:29.561
And then
for the rest of the show,

00:10:29.561 --> 00:10:31.096
Wally and I will just
play backgammon

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:33.932
while he holds up a cue card
reading, "Is the AC on?

00:10:33.932 --> 00:10:35.334
I'm boiling!"

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:38.503
And yet somehow, all of the
major Justice Department leaders

00:10:38.503 --> 00:10:39.972
